WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.525
A radar is only as good as the way it’s tuned, and three knobs do most of the work.

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:08.600
Gain is the overall sensitivity.

3
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.475
Too low, and you miss weak targets.

4
00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:14.575
Too high, and the screen fills with speckle.

5
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:21.100
Sea clutter control, also called S T C, cuts down the echoes from waves close to the boat.

6
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:26.700
Rain clutter control, F T C, breaks up the solid smear of a rain squall.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.200
Here’s the danger in all three.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.475
Turn them up too far, and what disappears along with the clutter?

9
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:36.250
The real targets.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.450
A small boat or a buoy looks just like clutter to the radar.

11
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.975
So use as little as you need.

12
00:00:43.225 --> 00:00:44.850
And the display.

13
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.425
Head-up puts your heading straight up.

14
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:53.950
North-up and course-up use a heading sensor to hold the picture steady, which makes plotting easier.
